1
00:00:03,068 --> 00:00:03,373
Yuck!

2
00:00:03,423 --> 00:00:05,716
Mila tastes a drop of sea: salty!

3
00:00:05,766 --> 00:00:08,557
Yet tap water and river water are fresh.

4
00:00:08,607 --> 00:00:10,098
Why is the sea salty?

5
00:00:10,888 --> 00:00:13,077
Noah tastes the stream: no salt.

6
00:00:13,127 --> 00:00:15,737
And yet, every stream and river flows…

7
00:00:15,787 --> 00:00:16,506
to the sea.

8
00:00:16,556 --> 00:00:17,116
Strange!

9
00:00:17,882 --> 00:00:19,396
Discovery mission!

10
00:00:21,912 --> 00:00:22,463
Mini mode!

11
00:00:22,513 --> 00:00:24,328
Rain is just a tiny bit acidic.

12
00:00:24,378 --> 00:00:25,471
Flowing over rocks,

13
00:00:25,521 --> 00:00:28,839
it wears them down and carries away tiny grains of salt.

14
00:00:28,889 --> 00:00:30,694
Too few to taste in the river!

15
00:00:31,505 --> 00:00:33,509
But day after day, for millions of years,

16
00:00:33,559 --> 00:00:35,263
rivers bring their salt to the sea.

17
00:00:35,313 --> 00:00:37,517
The water goes back up into the sky as vapor,

18
00:00:37,567 --> 00:00:39,771
without the salt: it stays, and it piles up.

19
00:00:40,530 --> 00:00:41,844
At the bottom of the sea,

20
00:00:41,894 --> 00:00:45,610
water heated by volcanoes comes back out full of minerals: more salt!

21
00:00:45,660 --> 00:00:45,991
In all,

22
00:00:46,041 --> 00:00:49,097
a glass of sea water holds almost two spoonfuls of salt.

23
00:00:49,871 --> 00:00:51,554
Two spoonfuls of salt in a glass:

24
00:00:51,604 --> 00:00:53,024
that's the taste of the sea.

25
00:00:53,074 --> 00:00:55,387
And since the water always leaves without it,

26
00:00:55,437 --> 00:00:56,697
the sea will stay salty.

27
00:00:57,498 --> 00:00:59,297
That's why the sea is salty.

28
00:01:01,025 --> 00:01:03,987
Rain wears down rocks, rivers carry the salt to the sea,

29
00:01:04,037 --> 00:01:05,759
and the water leaves without it.

30
00:01:06,984 --> 00:01:10,002
With an adult: put very salty water in a plate,

31
00:01:10,052 --> 00:01:10,720
in the sun.

32
00:01:10,770 --> 00:01:12,221
When the water is gone…

33
00:01:12,271 --> 00:01:13,838
the salt is still there!

34
00:01:14,611 --> 00:01:16,665
And why does the sea rise and fall?

35
00:01:16,715 --> 00:01:17,917
The answer tomorrow.
